# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# .env holds your Supabase URL and anon key locally. On GitHub Pages the
# same values are injected from repository secrets at build time, so this
# file exists only on your machine and must never be committed.
#
# The anon key is safe to expose publicly (it ships in the built bundle
# either way -- row-level security is what protects the data). This rule
# is here so that a service_role key, or anything else you add later,
# can never be committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Thousands of files, fully reproducible from package-lock.json via
# `npm ci`. Never committed.
node_modules/

# ─── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `npm run build` regenerates dist/ from source. The deploy workflow
# builds it on the runner and uploads it as a Pages artifact, so the
# repo never needs a copy.
dist/

# ─── Android / Capacitor ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `npx cap add android` writes its own .gitignore inside android/ that
# covers most of this. These entries are belt-and-braces for the ones
# that matter most:
#
#   local.properties  -- hardcodes the Android SDK path on THIS computer.
#                        Meaningless and actively wrong on any other
#                        machine, including a CI runner.
#   assets/public/    -- the copied web build, regenerated by `cap sync`.
#                        Committing it means every build shows up as a
#                        diff of minified bundles.
android/local.properties
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/

# ─── Signing keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The upload keystore signs your Play Store releases. If it leaks,
# someone else can sign builds as you; if you lose it, Play App Signing
# lets you recover -- but never commit it either way.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# ─── Editor and OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
supabase/.temp/
dist-native/  
